# apply-config.sh writes a timestamped capture/<UTC-timestamp>/ folder on every
# run (live-state capture + rendered-desired + diff + version-counts, for
# audit trail). These are generated artifacts, not source — never commit
# them. The durable rollback record is lifecycle-policy.json's own _comment
# block (committed, versioned) — not the commit message (round-1 finding I7:
# an earlier draft of README.md claimed it was; it wasn't).
capture/
